# 4. OPENING ANIMATION

When the guest first enters the menu, show the closed cover rather than immediately displaying menu items.

Create this opening sequence:

- The book cover appears centered.
- A subtle shadow establishes depth.
- The cover rotates around its edge.
- The first page or spread is revealed naturally.
- The book becomes ready for interaction.

Target an opening animation of approximately 700–1200 milliseconds.

Keep it smooth, natural, and premium.

Do not add long intro screens, unnecessary loading animations, sound effects, or excessive visual effects.

The guest should reach the actual menu quickly.

Respect reduced-motion preferences by providing a simpler opening transition when appropriate.

